  file_change {
    absolute_path_uri: "file:///NextJsGuide.md"
    file_change_type: FILE_CHANGE_TYPE_CREATE
    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "// Next.js Integration Guide\n\nThis file provides exactly what you requested: the terminal commands and the correct server-side structured code for **Next.js (App Router)** and **Prisma**. \n\nYou can preview the live visual dashboard implementation in the preview panel (which uses a Next.js-style component structure, ported to work in this live environment).\n\n### 1. Project Initialization Commands\n\nRun these terminal commands sequentially to bootstrap your Next.js project with Tailwind CSS and Prisma.\n\n```bash\n# 1. Initialize Next.js with App Router and Tailwind\nnpx create-next-app@latest admin-dashboard \\\n  --typescript --tailwind --eslint \\\n  --app --src-dir --import-alias \"@/*\"\n\n# Navigate into the directory\ncd admin-dashboard\n\n# 2. Install required icons and utilities\nnpm install lucide-react clsx tailwind-merge\n\n# 3. Install Prisma and initialize it\nnpm install prisma --save-dev\nnpm install @prisma/client\nnpx prisma init\n```\n\n*Note: Configure your database connection string in the newly created `.env` file generated by Prisma.*\n\n---\n\n### 2. Folder Structure\n\nHere is how you separate the React components from the Prisma logic:\n\n```\nadmin-dashboard/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 prisma/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 schema.prisma        <-- Define your User models here\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 app/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 layout.tsx       <-- Main dashboard layout (Sidebar included)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 page.tsx         <-- Next.js Server Component fetching Prisma\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 Sidebar.tsx      <-- Client-side / Static UI Component\n\342\224\202   \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 UserTable.tsx    <-- Client-side interactive table component\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 lib/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 prisma.ts        <-- Prisma Client singleton (separates DB logic)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Server Node Logic (`src/lib/prisma.ts`)\n\nKeep your database instantiation separate so you don\'t exhaust connection pools in development.\n\n```typescript\nimport { PrismaClient } from \'@prisma/client\'\n\nconst prismaClientSingleton = () => {\n  return new PrismaClient()\n}\n\ntype PrismaClientSingleton = ReturnType<typeof prismaClientSingleton>\n\nconst globalForPrisma = globalThis as unknown as {\n  prisma: PrismaClientSingleton | undefined\n}\n\nconst prisma = globalForPrisma.prisma ?? prismaClientSingleton()\n\nexport default prisma\n\nif (process.env.NODE_ENV !== \'production\') globalForPrisma.prisma = prisma\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Layout Code (`src/app/layout.tsx`)\n\nThis renders the sidebar globally for the dashboard. Note that we assume you are keeping root HTML tags in a parent `layout.tsx` or merging them.\n\n```tsx\nimport Sidebar from \'@/components/Sidebar\';\nimport \'./globals.css\';\n\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body className=\"flex h-screen bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 font-sans antialiased overflow-hidden\">\n        {/* Isolated Sidebar */}\n        <Sidebar />\n        \n        {/* Main Content Area */}\n        <main className=\"flex-1 flex flex-col overflow-hidden\">\n          {children}\n        </main>\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Page Code with Prisma Data Fetching (`src/app/page.tsx`)\n\nThis is a Next.js Server Component. It connects directly to Prisma securely on the server and passes the fetched payload to your interactive Client Component table.\n\n```tsx\nimport prisma from \'@/lib/prisma\';\nimport UserTable from \'@/components/UserTable\';\n// Assume you have an auth utility to get the session role\nimport { getUserSession } from \'@/lib/auth\'; \n\nexport const dynamic = \'force-dynamic\'; // Prevent caching for live admin data\n\nexport default async function UsersPage() {\n  // 1. Secure Database Data Fetch via Prisma\n  const users = await prisma.user.findMany({\n    select: {\n      id: true,\n      name: true,\n      email: true,\n      role: true,\n      status: true,\n    },\n    orderBy: { createdAt: \'desc\' }\n  });\n\n  // 2. Fetch the current logged-in user\'s session role (e.g., via NextAuth)\n  const session = await getUserSession();\n  const currentUserRole = session?.role || \'Admin\';\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <header className=\"bg-white border-b border-slate-200 px-8 py-5\">\n        <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-800\">User Management</h1>\n        <p className=\"text-slate-500 text-sm mt-1\">Manage system administrators and operator access.</p>\n      </header>\n      \n      <div className=\"p-8 flex-1 overflow-y-auto\">\n         {/* Pass server-fetched data and securely fetched role to the Client UI */}\n         <UserTable initialUsers={users} currentUserRole={currentUserRole} />\n      </div>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Secure Server Action (`src/app/actions.ts`)\n\nTo ensure **secure server-side role validation** when deleting a user (so they can\'t just bypass the UI hidden buttons), define a Next.js Server Action:\n\n```typescript\n\'use server\'\n\nimport prisma from \'@/lib/prisma\';\nimport { getUserSession } from \'@/lib/auth\';\nimport { revalidatePath } from \'next/cache\';\n\nexport async function deleteUserAction(userId: number) {\n  // 1. Re-validate role securely on the server\n  const session = await getUserSession();\n  \n  if (session?.role !== \'Superadmin\') {\n    throw new Error(\'Unauthorized: Only Superadmins can delete users.\');\n  }\n\n  // 2. Safely perform Prisma deletion\n  await prisma.user.delete({\n    where: { id: userId }\n  });\n\n  // 3. Clear Next.js cache for the layout so the table updates\n  revalidatePath(\'/\');\n}\n```\n\n*(You would import this Server Action into the `UserTable` Client Component to hook up to the delete button).*"
    }
