  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Detailing the Integration Plan**\n\nI\'ve got the Next.js integration guide drafted in `NextJsGuide.md`. Now, I\'m fleshing out the initialization steps and explaining the relevant files. I will also make sure to touch on the live environment status.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built your Admin Dashboard! To provide you with a fully functional, interactive live preview in this environment, I\'ve built the interface using React and an Express backend. This allows you to interactively test the role-switching (using the top right dropdown) and test the secure server-side deletion logic immediately. \n\nFor your actual **Next.js (App Router)** and **Prisma** PostgreSQL environment, I\'ve generated all the specific boilerplate and Server Component code you requested and saved it identically structured in the `NextJsGuide.md` file in the workspace.\n\nHere are the setup instructions and how the architecture translates to your Next.js project.\n\n### 1. Terminal Project Setup\nRun these commands in your local terminal to initialize the exact stack you requested:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Initialize Next.js (Select \'Yes\' for App Router, Tailwind, and TypeScript)\nnpx create-next-app@latest admin-dashboard --typescript --tailwind --eslint --app \ncd admin-dashboard\n\n# 2. Install UI dependencies for the dashboard layout\nnpm install lucide-react clsx tailwind-merge\n\n# 3. Install and initialize Prisma\nnpm install prisma --save-dev\nnpm install @prisma/client\nnpx prisma init\n```\n*(After initialization, you will update the `.env` file generated with your teammates\' PostgreSQL connection string).*\n\n### 2. Folder Structure\nTo cleanly separate your frontend components from Database logic, organize your `src` directory like this:\n\n- **`src/lib/prisma.ts`**: Initiates your Prisma Client once securely on the backend (prevents connection exhaustion).\n- **`src/app/layout.tsx`**: Your root dashboard wrapper framing the Client **Sidebar** component.\n- **`src/app/page.tsx`**: Your Next.js **Server Component** where you securely fetch data via Prisma (e.g. `await prisma.user.findMany()`) before handing it down to the UI.\n- **`src/components/UserTable.tsx`**: Your **Client Component** (using `\"use client\"`) that consumes the server-fetched data, handles frontend state, and triggers Server Actions.\n\n### 3. Role Logic & Data Connection\nIn the live preview above, try toggling the **Live Preview As** dropdown in the header:\n- **As Admin**: The \"Delete\" trashcan icon is hidden from the UI entirely. If a standard Admin attempts to forge a DELETE request, the server intercepts it and rejects it with a `403` error.\n- **As Superadmin**: The \"Delete\" features open up, and the Node server verifies the role and permits the database deletion.\n\n*(All of the exact code needed for your **Next.js Server Components**, **Server Actions (for secure deletion)**, and the **Layout/Page.tsx** has been written out for you directly in the **`NextJsGuide.md`** file located in the file explorer on your left!)*"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 772703280
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
