  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying the Inquiry**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s initial questions. It appears they\'re aiming to understand how to upload unzipped code to GitHub, specifically concerning permissions and collaboration with teammates. I\'m prioritizing understanding their exact setup and constraints to offer a precise response.\n\n\n**Addressing the Connection**\n\nI\'ve formulated a complete set of instructions for pushing the unzipped code to GitHub, including initialization, committing, and remote setup. I\'m also confirming the app is ready for a real database connection. I am ready to begin summarizing the project now.\n\n\n**Summarizing the Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing the functional aspects of the website, like authentication (including role-based access), the user management system (with filtering and deletion based on role), and a user provisioning system. I\'m also including detailed features, such as real-time auditing and security notifications. The setup is also ready for a database connection.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Yes, you can absolutely push the downloaded code to GitHub, and your teammates will have everything they need to connect it to a real database.\n\nHere are the answers to your questions, followed by the summaries you requested:\n\n### Pushing to GitHub\nOnce you unzip the downloaded file, open your terminal (or command prompt), navigate into the unzipped folder, and run these commands to push it to a new GitHub repository:\n\n1. **Initialize Git:** `git init`\n2. **Add all files:** `git add .`\n3. **Commit the code:** `git commit -m \"Initial commit from AI Studio\"`\n4. **Link to GitHub:** Create a new, empty repository on GitHub. Copy its URL, then run: `git remote add origin <YOUR_GITHUB_REPO_URL>`\n5. **Push the code:** `git push -u origin main` (or `master` depending on your default branch name).\n\n### Connecting a Real Database\n**Yes, your teammates are perfectly set up to connect a real database.** \nThe code currently uses an Express backend with a simulated array of users to provide a live preview. However, I have already included a file named `NextJsGuide.md` directly in your downloaded codebase. This file contains step-by-step instructions and production-ready code snippets specifically showing your teammates how to initialize **Prisma ORM**, connect a real SQL database (like PostgreSQL or MySQL), and replace the dummy data with real server queries.\n\n***\n\n### \360\237\223\213 Website Functions Summary\n\nHere is a high-level overview of the functional modules built into the LivestockGuard Admin application:\n\n* **Role-Based Authentication (RBAC):** A secure login portal that routes users into the system. The entire application conditionally renders based on whether the active user is an **Admin** or a **Superadmin**.\n* **Enterprise Dashboard:** A data visualization layer displaying system-wide metrics (Total Users, Active Sessions, Admin Counts) with real-time metric cards.\n* **Directory & User Management:** An interactive data table allowing administrators to view, filter, and manage staff. **Superadmins** have exclusive privileges to delete accounts.\n* **Secure User Provisioning:** A dedicated form to onboard new operators and admins, featuring password strength requirements and backend system constraints (e.g., strictly enforcing a maximum of one Super Admin system-wide).\n* **Auditing & Reports:** \n    * **Superadmins** see real-time sessions of other online admins and critical global security alerts (like unauthorized access attempts).\n    * **Admins** see operational field data and standard user-management audit logs.\n* **System Settings & Preferences:** A multi-tab configuration interface allowing users to manage their Profile Details, set up SMS/Email Notification triggers, view Security roles, and manage external system API Keys.\n\n***\n\n### \360\237\223\235 GitHub Repository Description\n\nYou can copy and paste this directly into your GitHub repository\'s \"About\" or `README.md` description:\n\n> **LivestockGuard Enterprise Admin Portal**\n> A secure, role-based administration dashboard designed for livestock monitoring operations. This application features strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), secure user provisioning, real-time audit logging, and actionable security portals for managing field operators and system administrators. Built with React, Tailwind CSS, and structured for easy integration with Prisma and SQL databases."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 243828713
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
