ps for database integration, highlighting the existing mock database and emphasizing the ease of swapping it with a real database. I\'m recommending Prisma as an ORM and providing installation commands. I\'m also instructing the user to update the `.env` file with their database string, and finally to replace the mock database operations in `server.ts` with Prisma queries.\n\n\n**Securing the Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now integrating JWT validation into the `authenticateRole` middleware within `server.ts`. I\'m going to leverage a library like `jsonwebtoken` for secure endpoint access. The goal is to enforce role-based access control by verifying JWT tokens. I\'ll need to configure this middleware to validate tokens and determine user roles for authorization. This will ensure that only authorized users can access sensitive endpoints.\n\n\n**Generating the Team Guide**\n\nI\'m now generating a `TEAM_GUIDE.md` file, although I\'ll overwrite the standard `README.md` to ensure it\'s present. I\'m focusing on the GitHub repository description, aiming for a concise explanation. The description will be \"A secure, role-based enterprise administration dashboard for livestock monitoring and field operator management.\" I\'m also including information about API keys, explaining their purpose for enabling external systems to interact with the database autonomously. I plan to create the comprehensive file and output conceptual responses adhering to communication guidelines.\n\n\n"
