  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have created a comprehensive `README.md` file right in the root of your project files. When you extract your downloaded ZIP, that file will be there to serve as a complete guide for your development team. \n\nTo answer your questions directly:\n\n*   **Can you open it in VS Code?** Yes. Once you unzip the folder, open your terminal, navigate inside the folder, and simply type `code .` to open it in VS Code.\n*   **Pushing to GitHub:** Yes, it is fully ready to be pushed. You just need to initialize git (`git init`), commit the files (`git commit`), and push to your new GitHub repository URL. (I\'ve included the exact terminal commands for your team in the `README.md`).\n*   **Connecting a Real Database:** Absolutely. Right now, the backend uses an Express server (`server.ts`) with local mock data so you can test the UI functionality. Your backend team just needs to install a database client (like Prisma or Mongoose), connect their database URL, and replace the mock array in `server.ts` with real database queries. \n*   **What are API Keys for?** API keys act as secure, machine-to-machine passwords. They allow external hardware or software\342\200\224like IoT cattle tracking collars, automated farming equipment, or external analytics tools\342\200\224to securely send and receive data from your application without requiring human login credentials.\n\n**GitHub Repository Description:**\n> \"A secure, role-based enterprise administration dashboard for livestock monitoring and field operator management.\"\n\n**Website Functions Summary:**\n*   **Role-Based Access Control:** Strict handling of privileges for standard Operators, basic Admins, and a strictly enforced single Super Admin.\n*   **User Management:** Complete real-time interface for adding, removing, and defining roles for enterprise personnel.\n*   **Reporting & Auditing:** Comprehensive dashboards detailing active field users, real-time administrator sessions, and critical security logs.\n*   **System Configuration:** Detailed settings modules for profile management, notification preference routing, credential updates, and API key lifecycle management."
